**Blocking finding:** the run establishes roughly 210 seconds of overhead outside the agent clock. It does **not** establish that the official scorer intrinsically pays that cost, or that wheel construction causes it. The kernel adds dependency setup that the stock subprocess backend skips, then discards its execution result. That leaves the likely expensive command unobserved. [agent_timing.py:90](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/eval/kaggle/agent_timing.py:90), [container_setup.py:529](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/container_setup.py:529)

The strongest case **against cutting the cap to 1.4 minutes now** is therefore measurement validity: the timing kernel has a concrete path to repeated offline pip retries that need not occur in the scorer’s Docker image. The approved interim gate remains prudent while that is unresolved. [decision 022:9](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/ops/decisions/022-003-e4b-v000-timing-gate-fail.md:9)

